-- title:
--   Fontaine's lifting criterion for maps from F[p^v]
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel $(p)$, and complete for the $(p)$-adic topology. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional commutative formal group law over $\mathcal O$ (a $d$-tuple of power series in $2d$ variables with vanishing constant terms, linear terms $A_i+B_i$, associative and symmetric). Let $F_p$ be a $d$-tuple of series with vanishing constant terms whose coefficients satisfy $c_m(F_p)\,p=p^{\deg m}c_m(F)$ for $m\neq 0$ (the rescaled law $F(pA,pB)/p$), and let $\varphi,\psi$ be $d$-tuples of series in $d$ variables with vanishing constant terms, the linear part of $\varphi$ the identity matrix, all coefficients of $\varphi$ and of $\psi$ lying in $(p^N)$ outside a finite set of multi-indices for each $N$, $\varphi\circ F_p=\varphi(A)+\varphi(B)$, and $\psi\circ\varphi=\varphi\circ\psi=X$. Let $v\in\mathbb N$ and let $R$ be a commutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module, with $R$ and $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ $(p)$-adically complete, together with a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi:\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to R$ such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)$, $\pi$ coincides with $(p)$-adic evaluation at the family $(\pi(X_i))_i$, $\ker\pi$ is generated by the $d$ components of the $p^v$-th iterate $[p^v]_F$ of $F$ (the series defined by $s_0=0$, $s_{n+1,i}=F_i(s_n,X)$), and $\Delta(\pi(X_i))$ is the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $F_i$ at $(\pi(X_j)\otimes 1,\,1\otimes\pi(X_j))$ in $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$. Assume the Cartier dual $\mathrm{Dual}_{\mathbb Z/p}(\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R)$ is a local ring. Let $Y$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module, and let $\chi:\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}Y$ be a $\mathbb Z/p$-algebra map such that for every $n$ and every additive element $m$ of the truncated Witt vectors of length $n$ over $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ (that is, $W_n(\Delta)m=W_n(\mathrm{incl}_L)m+W_n(\mathrm{incl}_R)m$): if $m$ is the length-$n$ truncation of $W(\iota_R)(\tilde m)$ for some Witt vector $\tilde m$ over $R$ whose $(n-1)$-st ghost component lies in $(p^n)R$, where $\iota_R:R\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ is the right inclusion, then $W_n(\chi)(m)$ satisfies the same condition relative to $\iota_Y:Y\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}Y$. Then there exists an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $x:R\to Y$ with $\mathrm{id}_{\mathbb Z/p}\otimes x=\chi$. No uniqueness is asserted.
--
--   This is the finite-level form of Fontaine's criterion: a map on special fibres which respects his condition on homomorphisms to the Witt vector groups lifts to the integral models, stated here for the $p^v$-torsion of a unipotent commutative formal group law presented by an explicit integral logarithm package $(F_p,\varphi,\psi)$. It is used by [`Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp), which feeds the classification of finite flat group schemes entering the local analysis of the Galois deformation rings.
